{"id":"mahabharata-7-122","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":122,"title":"द्वाविंशत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 122 · The Kauravas after Jayadratha's fall","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra asks what his men did after Jayadratha fell, and Sanjaya tells how Arjuna and Krishna met the Kaurava warriors who attacked them in anger. Drona's son and others charge at Arjuna, and Krishna directs the horses against Somadatta's son.","kn":"ಜಯದ್ರಥ ಬಿದ್ದ ಮೇಲೆ ತನ್ನ ಜನ ಏನು ಮಾಡಿದರೆಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕೋಪದಿಂದ ಎರಗಿದ ಕೌರವ ವೀರರನ್ನು ಅರ್ಜುನ-ಕೃಷ್ಣರು ಎದುರಿಸಿದ್ದನ್ನು ಸಂಜಯ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮಾದಿಗಳು ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಸೋಮದತ್ತನ ಮಗನ ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಕುದುರೆ ನಡೆಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र पूछते हैं कि जयद्रथ के गिरने पर उनके योद्धाओं ने क्या किया, और संजय बताते हैं कि क्रोध से आक्रमण करते कौरव वीरों का सामना अर्जुन-कृष्ण ने कैसे किया। अश्वत्थामा आदि अर्जुन पर टूटते हैं, और कृष्ण सोमदत्त के पुत्र की ओर घोड़े मोड़ते हैं।","te":"జయద్రథుడు పడిన తరువాత తన వారు ఏం చేశారని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు అడుగుతాడు; కోపంతో దాడి చేసిన కౌరవ వీరులను అర్జున కృష్ణులు ఎదుర్కొన్నారని సంజయుడు చెబుతాడు. అశ్వత్థామ తదితరులు అర్జునునిపై దూకుతారు; కృష్ణుడు సోమదత్తుని కుమారుని వైపు గుర్రాలను నడుపుతాడు.","ta":"ஜயத்ரதன் வீழ்ந்தபின் தன் வீரர் என்ன செய்தனர் என்று த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் கேட்கிறான்; சினத்துடன் தாக்கிய கௌரவ வீரரை அர்ஜுனனும் கண்ணனும் எதிர்கொண்டதைச் சஞ்சயன் கூறுகிறான். அஸ்வத்தாமன் முதலியோர் அர்ஜுனனைத் தாக்க, கண்ணன் சோமதத்தனின் மகனை நோக்கிக் குதிரைகளைச் செலுத்துகிறார்.","ml":"ജയദ്രഥൻ വീണശേഷം തന്റെ ആളുകൾ എന്തു ചെയ്തുവെന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; കോപത്തോടെ ആക്രമിച്ച കൗരവ യോദ്ധാക്കളെ അർജുനനും കൃഷ്ണനും നേരിട്ടത് സഞ്ജയൻ പറയുന്നു. ദ്രോണരുടെ പുത്രനും മറ്റുള്ളവരും അർജുനനെ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു; സോമദത്തന്റെ പുത്രനു നേരെ കൃഷ്ണൻ കുതിരകളെ തിരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.122; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"घटोत्कचवधपर्व","titleEn":"Ghatotkachavadha Parva (Slaying of Ghatotkacha)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तस्मिन्विनिहते वीरे सैन्धवे सव्यसाचिना ।\nमामका यदकुर्वन्त तन्ममाचक्ष्व संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the hero Saindhava had been killed by Savyasachin, tell me, Sanjaya, what my men did."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"सैन्धवं निहतं दृष्ट्वा रणे पार्थेन मारिष ।\nअमर्षवशमापन्नः कृपः शारद्वतस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Saindhava killed in battle by Partha, honorable sir, Kripa son of Sharadvat was seized by fury."}},{"n":3,"text":"महता शरवर्षेण पाण्डवं समवाकिरत् ।\nद्रौणिश्चाभ्यद्रवत्पार्थं रथमास्थाय फल्गुनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He covered the Pandava with a great shower of arrows, and Drona's son too, mounting his chariot, rushed at Phalguna Partha."}},{"n":4,"text":"तावेनं रथिनां श्रेष्ठौ रथाभ्यां रथसत्तमम् ।\nउभावुभयतस्तीक्ष्णैर्विशिखैरभ्यवर्षताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two best of chariot-fighters, from two chariots, rained sharp arrows on that excellent chariot-warrior from both sides."}},{"n":5,"text":"स तथा शरवर्षाभ्यां सुमहद्भ्यां महाभुजः ।\nपीड्यमानः परामार्तिमगमद्रथिनां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pressed by those two huge showers of arrows, the mighty-armed best of charioteers suffered great pain."}},{"n":6,"text":"सोऽजिघांसुर्गुरुं संख्ये गुरोस्तनयमेव च ।\nचकाराचार्यकं तत्र कुन्तीपुत्रो धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Kunti's son Dhananjaya, not wishing to kill his teacher or his teacher's son, acted as a pupil would there."}},{"n":7,"text":"अस्त्रैरस्त्राणि संवार्य द्रौणेः शारद्वतस्य च ।\nमन्दवेगानिषूंस्ताभ्यामजिघांसुरवासृजत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Warding off the weapons of Drona's son and of Sharadvat's son with his own weapons, he shot at them slow arrows, wishing not to kill them."}},{"n":8,"text":"ते नातिभृशमभ्यघ्नन्विशिखा जयचोदिताः ।\nबहुत्वात्तु परामार्तिं शराणां तावगच्छताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Driven by his wish for victory, those arrows did not strike very hard, but through their very number the two felt great pain."}},{"n":9,"text":"अथ शारद्वतो राजन्कौन्तेयशरपीडितः ।\nअवासीदद्रथोपस्थे मूर्च्छामभिजगाम ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Sharadvat's son, pressed by the arrows of Kunti's son, sank down on the seat of his chariot, O king, and fainted."}},{"n":10,"text":"विह्वलं तमभिज्ञाय भर्तारं शरपीडितम् ।\nहतोऽयमिति च ज्ञात्वा सारथिस्तमपावहत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing his master distressed and wounded by arrows, and thinking he was dead, the charioteer carried him away."}},{"n":11,"text":"तस्मिन्सन्ने महाराज कृपे शारद्वते युधि ।\nअश्वत्थामाप्यपायासीत्पाण्डवेयाद्रथान्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Kripa son of Sharadvat had collapsed in the fight, O great king, Ashvatthama too left the Pandava's chariot."}},{"n":12,"text":"दृष्ट्वा शारद्वतं पार्थो मूर्छितं शरपीडितम् ।\nरथ एव महेष्वासः कृपणं पर्यदेवयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Sharadvat's son fainting, pierced by arrows, Partha the great bowman, standing on his chariot, lamented pitifully."}},{"n":13,"text":"पश्यन्निदं महाप्राज्ञः क्षत्ता राजानमुक्तवान् ।\nकुलान्तकरणे पापे जातमात्रे सुयोधने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Foreseeing this, the wise Kshatta said to the king, when Suyodhana had just been born, the destroyer of the family and a sinner:"}},{"n":14,"text":"नीयतां परलोकाय साध्वयं कुलपांसनः ।\nअस्माद्धि कुरुमुख्यानां महदुत्पत्स्यते भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Take this scourge of his family away to the other world, it would be good, for from him great fear will arise for the chief Kurus.'"}},{"n":15,"text":"तदिदं समनुप्राप्तं वचनं सत्यवादिनः ।\nतत्कृते ह्यद्य पश्यामि शरतल्पगतं कृपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That word of the truth-speaker has now come true, for because of him I see Kripa today lying on a bed of arrows."}},{"n":16,"text":"धिगस्तु क्षात्रमाचारं धिगस्तु बलपौरुषम् ।\nको हि ब्राह्मणमाचार्यमभिद्रुह्येत मादृशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shame on the warrior's code, shame on strength and manliness! For who like me would turn against a Brahmin, a teacher?"}},{"n":17,"text":"ऋषिपुत्रो ममाचार्यो द्रोणस्य दयितः सखा ।\nएष शेते रथोपस्थे मद्बाणैरभिपीडितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is the son of a sage, my teacher, Drona's dear friend. Here he lies on the chariot-seat, tormented by my arrows."}},{"n":18,"text":"अकामयानेन मया विशिखैरर्दितो भृशम् ।\nअवासीदद्रथोपस्थे प्राणान्पीडयतीव मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I did not want it, yet he was greatly pained by my arrows, and he sank down on the chariot-seat as if my arrows were crushing his life."}},{"n":19,"text":"शरार्दितेन हि मया प्रेक्षणीयो महाद्युतिः ।\nप्रत्यस्तो बहुभिर्बाणैर्दशधर्मगतेन वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pierced by my many arrows, the radiant man is a sight to see, fallen into that wretched state."}},{"n":20,"text":"शोचयत्येष निपतन्भूयः पुत्रवधाद्धि माम् ।\nकृपणं स्वरथे सन्नं पश्य कृष्ण यथा गतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he falls, he makes me grieve again as I grieved for my son's death. Look, Krishna, at how the poor man lies sunk on his chariot."}},{"n":21,"text":"उपाकृत्य तु वै विद्यामाचार्येभ्यो नरर्षभाः ।\nप्रयच्छन्तीह ये कामान्देवत्वमुपयान्ति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The best of men who give their pupils the learning they have received from teachers, and grant their wishes, become gods."}},{"n":22,"text":"ये तु विद्यामुपादाय गुरुभ्यः पुरुषाधमाः ।\nघ्नन्ति तानेव दुर्वृत्तास्ते वै निरयगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But base men who take learning from their teachers and then strike them, wicked ones, go to hell."}},{"n":23,"text":"तदिदं नरकायाद्य कृतं कर्म मया ध्रुवम् ।\nआचार्यं शरवर्षेण रथे सादयता कृपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely today I have done a deed that leads to hell, in making the teacher Kripa sink down in his chariot with a shower of arrows."}},{"n":24,"text":"यत्तत्पूर्वमुपाकुर्वन्नस्त्रं मामब्रवीत्कृपः ।\nन कथंचन कौरव्य प्रहर्तव्यं गुराविति ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he was first teaching me the weapon, Kripa told me: 'Descendant of Kuru, on no account should you strike a teacher.'"}},{"n":25,"text":"तदिदं वचनं साधोराचार्यस्य महात्मनः ।\nनानुष्ठितं तमेवाजौ विशिखैरभिवर्षता ॥","meaning":{"en":"That counsel of the good and great teacher has not been followed by me, who rained arrows on him in this fight."}},{"n":26,"text":"नमस्तस्मै सुपूज्याय गौतमायापलायिने ।\nधिगस्तु मम वार्ष्णेय यो ह्यस्मै प्रहराम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Homage to that most worthy Gautama who does not flee! Shame on me, Vrishni, who strike him.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"तथा विलपमाने तु सव्यसाचिनि तं प्रति ।\nसैन्धवं निहतं दृष्ट्वा राधेयः समुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Savyasachin was lamenting so over him, Radheya, seeing Saindhava dead, rushed up."}},{"n":28,"text":"उपायान्तं तु राधेयं दृष्ट्वा पार्थो महारथः ।\nप्रहसन्देवकीपुत्रमिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Radheya approach, the great chariot-warrior Partha, laughing, said this to Devaki's son."}},{"n":29,"text":"एष प्रयात्याधिरथिः सात्यकेः स्यन्दनं प्रति ।\nन मृष्यति हतं नूनं भूरिश्रवसमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Here goes Adhiratha's son toward Satyaki's chariot. He cannot bear that Bhurishravas was killed in the battle."}},{"n":30,"text":"यत्र यात्येष तत्र त्वं चोदयाश्वाञ्जनार्दन ।\nमा सोमदत्तेः पदवीं गमयेत्सात्यकिं वृषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wherever he goes, Janardana, drive the horses there, so that Karna does not send Satyaki along the path of Somadatta's son.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"एवमुक्तो महाबाहुः केशवः सव्यसाचिना ।\nप्रत्युवाच महातेजाः कालयुक्तमिदं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to so by Savyasachin, mighty-armed and mighty-radiant Keshava answered with words suited to the time."}},{"n":32,"text":"अलमेष महाबाहुः कर्णायैको हि पाण्डव ।\nकिं पुनर्द्रौपदेयाभ्यां सहितः सात्वतर्षभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This mighty-armed Pandava is enough, alone, for Karna; and what of the bull of the Satvatas joined by the two sons of Draupadi?"}},{"n":33,"text":"न च तावत्क्षमः पार्थ कर्णेन तव संगरः ।\nप्रज्वलन्ती महोल्केव तिष्ठत्यस्य हि वासवी ।\nत्वदर्थं पूज्यमानैषा रक्ष्यते परवीरहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your fight with Karna is not yet suitable, Partha. Indra's spear stands blazing like a great meteor in his hand; it is honored and kept for your sake, slayer of enemy heroes."}},{"n":34,"text":"अतः कर्णः प्रयात्वत्र सात्वतस्य यथा तथा ।\nअहं ज्ञास्यामि कौरव्य कालमस्य दुरात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So let Karna go there, as it may be, against the Satvata. I shall know the time for that wicked one, descendant of Kuru.\""}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":35,"text":"योऽसौ कर्णेन वीरेण वार्ष्णेयस्य समागमः ।\nहते तु भूरिश्रवसि सैन्धवे च निपातिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the hero Karna and Vrishni's descendant met, after Bhurishravas was slain and Saindhava had fallen,"}},{"n":36,"text":"सात्यकिश्चापि विरथः कं समारूढवान्रथम् ।\nचक्ररक्षौ च पाञ्चाल्यौ तन्ममाचक्ष्व संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"what chariot did the chariotless Satyaki mount, and the two wheel-guards of Panchala? Tell me that, Sanjaya."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":37,"text":"हन्त ते वर्णयिष्यामि यथावृत्तं महारणे ।\nशुश्रूषस्व स्थिरो भूत्वा दुराचरितमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear, I shall tell you how it happened in that great battle; listen steadily to the misdeed of your own side."}},{"n":38,"text":"पूर्वमेव हि कृष्णस्य मनोगतमिदं प्रभो ।\nविजेतव्यो यथा वीरः सात्यकिर्यूपकेतुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even before, this was in Krishna's mind: that the hero Satyaki should be overcome by the man with the sacrificial-post banner."}},{"n":39,"text":"अतीतानागतं राजन्स हि वेत्ति जनार्दनः ।\nअतः सूतं समाहूय दारुकं संदिदेश ह ।\nरथो मे युज्यतां काल्यमिति राजन्महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Janardana knows past and future, O king, so he called his charioteer Daruka and commanded him: 'Let my chariot be yoked at dawn,' that mighty man said."}},{"n":40,"text":"न हि देवा न गन्धर्वा न यक्षोरगराक्षसाः ।\nमानवा वा विजेतारः कृष्णयोः सन्ति केचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"For neither gods, gandharvas, yakshas, serpents, rakshasas nor men can defeat the two Krishnas."}},{"n":41,"text":"पितामहपुरोगाश्च देवाः सिद्धाश्च तं विदुः ।\nतयोः प्रभावमतुलं शृणु युद्धं च तद्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods led by Brahma and the Siddhas know them. Hear their matchless power and how that battle went."}},{"n":42,"text":"सात्यकिं विरथं दृष्ट्वा कर्णं चाभ्युद्यतायुधम् ।\nदध्मौ शङ्खं महावेगमार्षभेणाथ माधवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Satyaki chariotless and Karna with weapon raised, Madhava blew his conch with a great, bull-like blast."}},{"n":43,"text":"दारुकोऽवेत्य संदेशं श्रुत्वा शङ्खस्य च स्वनम् ।\nरथमन्वानयत्तस्मै सुपर्णोच्छ्रितकेतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Daruka, understanding the order and hearing the conch's sound, brought a chariot to him with a banner raised high with Garuda on it."}},{"n":44,"text":"स केशवस्यानुमते रथं दारुकसंयुतम् ।\nआरुरोह शिनेः पौत्रो ज्वलनादित्यसंनिभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With Keshava's leave, Shini's grandson mounted that chariot with Daruka, bright as fire and sun."}},{"n":45,"text":"कामगैः सैन्यसुग्रीवमेघपुष्पबलाहकैः ।\nहयोदग्रैर्महावेगैर्हेमभाण्डविभूषितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was drawn by horses named Saivya, Sugriva, Megha-pushpa and Balahaka, swift as thought, tall, fast, adorned with golden trappings."}},{"n":46,"text":"युक्तं समारुह्य च तं विमानप्रतिमं रथम् ।\nअभ्यद्रवत राधेयं प्रवपन्सायकान्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mounting that chariot, which was like a heavenly car, he rushed against Radheya, showering many arrows."}},{"n":47,"text":"चक्ररक्षावपि तदा युधामन्यूत्तमौजसौ ।\nधनंजयरथं हित्वा राधेयं प्रत्युदीययुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two wheel-guards, Yudhamanyu and Uttamaujas, then left Dhananjaya's chariot and went toward Radheya."}},{"n":48,"text":"राधेयोऽपि महाराज शरवर्षं समुत्सृजन् ।\nअभ्यद्रवत्सुसंक्रुद्धो रणे शैनेयमच्युतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Radheya too, O great king, pouring down arrows, rushed in great anger against Shaineya, the unfailing."}},{"n":49,"text":"नैव दैवं न गान्धर्वं नासुरोरगराक्षसम् ।\nतादृशं भुवि वा युद्धं दिवि वा श्रुतमित्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"A battle like that was not heard of among gods, gandharvas, asuras, serpents or rakshasas, on earth or in heaven."}},{"n":50,"text":"उपारमत तत्सैन्यं सरथाश्वनरद्विपम् ।\nतयोर्दृष्ट्वा महाराज कर्म संमूढचेतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your army, with chariots, horses, men and elephants, stopped, its mind confused at seeing the deeds of those two, O great king."}},{"n":51,"text":"सर्वे च समपश्यन्त तद्युद्धमतिमानुषम् ।\nतयोर्नृवरयो राजन्सारथ्यं दारुकस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"All watched that superhuman battle, and the charioteering of Daruka for those two best of men, O king,"}},{"n":52,"text":"गतप्रत्यागतावृत्तैर्मण्डलैः संनिवर्तनैः ।\nसारथेस्तु रथस्थस्य काश्यपेयस्य विस्मिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"by his forward and backward runs, his circling and turning, the charioteer of Kashyapa's line astonished them as he stood on the chariot."}},{"n":53,"text":"नभस्तलगताश्चैव देवगन्धर्वदानवाः ।\nअतीवावहिता द्रष्टुं कर्णशैनेययो रणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gods, gandharvas and danavas in the sky were most attentive to watch the fight of Karna and Shaineya."}},{"n":54,"text":"मित्रार्थे तौ पराक्रान्तौ स्पर्धिनौ शुष्मिणौ रणे ।\nकर्णश्चामरसंकाशो युयुधानश्च सात्यकिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two fought bravely for their friends, rivals in battle and mighty: Karna, like an immortal, and Yuyudhana Satyaki."}},{"n":55,"text":"अन्योन्यं तौ महाराज शरवर्षैरवर्षताम् ।\nप्रममाथ शिनेः पौत्रं कर्णः सायकवृष्टिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They showered each other with arrow-showers, O great king, and Karna crushed Shini's grandson with sheets of arrows."}},{"n":56,"text":"अमृष्यमाणो निधनं कौरव्यजलसंधयोः ।\nकर्णः शोकसमाविष्टो महोरग इव श्वसन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unable to bear the death of the Kuru and Jalasandha, Karna, filled with grief and hissing like a great serpent,"}},{"n":57,"text":"स शैनेयं रणे क्रुद्धः प्रदहन्निव चक्षुषा ।\nअभ्यद्रवत वेगेन पुनः पुनररिंदमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"angry, as if burning Shaineya with his glance, rushed at him again and again with speed, the scourge of foes."}},{"n":58,"text":"तं तु संप्रेक्ष्य संक्रुद्धं सात्यकिः प्रत्यविध्यत ।\nमहता शरवर्षेण गजः प्रतिगजं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him enraged, Satyaki struck back with a great shower of arrows, as an elephant fights a rival elephant."}},{"n":59,"text":"तौ समेत्य नरव्याघ्रौ व्याघ्राविव तरस्विनौ ।\nअन्योन्यं संततक्षाते रणेऽनुपमविक्रमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two tigers among men came together like two fierce tigers and tore at each other in battle, of unmatched valor."}},{"n":60,"text":"ततः कर्णं शिनेः पौत्रः सर्वपारशवैः शरैः ।\nबिभेद सर्वगात्रेषु पुनः पुनररिंदमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shini's grandson, the scourge of foes, pierced Karna again and again in all his limbs with arrows made of all iron."}},{"n":61,"text":"सारथिं चास्य भल्लेन रथनीडादपाहरत् ।\nअश्वांश्च चतुरः श्वेतान्निजघ्ने निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With a broad arrow he took the charioteer from the chariot's seat, and killed the four white horses with sharp arrows."}},{"n":62,"text":"छित्त्वा ध्वजं शतेनैव शतधा पुरुषर्षभः ।\nचकार विरथं कर्णं तव पुत्रस्य पश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cutting his banner in a hundred pieces with a hundred arrows, that bull among men made Karna chariotless in front of your son."}},{"n":63,"text":"ततो विमनसो राजंस्तावकाः पुरुषर्षभाः ।\nवृषसेनः कर्णसुतः शल्यो मद्राधिपस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your men, bulls among men, dispirited, Vrishasena Karna's son and Shalya king of Madra,"}},{"n":64,"text":"द्रोणपुत्रश्च शैनेयं सर्वतः पर्यवारयन् ।\nततः पर्याकुलं सर्वं न प्राज्ञायत किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"and Drona's son surrounded Shaineya on all sides. Then all was confused, and nothing could be made out."}},{"n":65,"text":"तथा सात्यकिना वीरे विरथे सूतजे कृते ।\nहाहाकारस्ततो राजन्सर्वसैन्येषु चाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the hero Satyaki had made the charioteer's son chariotless, a cry of woe rose throughout all the armies, O king."}},{"n":66,"text":"कर्णोऽपि विह्वलो राजन्सात्वतेनार्दितः शरैः ।\nदुर्योधनरथं राजन्नारुरोह विनिःश्वसन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna too, shaken and hurt by the Satvata's arrows, O king, sighed and climbed onto Duryodhana's chariot."}},{"n":67,"text":"मानयंस्तव पुत्रस्य बाल्यात्प्रभृति सौहृदम् ।\nकृतां राज्यप्रदानेन प्रतिज्ञां परिपालयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honoring his friendship with your son from boyhood and keeping the promise made when the kingdom was given him,"}},{"n":68,"text":"तथा तु विरथे कर्णे पुत्रान्वै तव पार्थिव ।\nदुःशासनमुखाञ्शूरान्नावधीत्सात्यकिर्वशी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki, self-controlled, did not kill your sons, heroes led by Duhshasana, though Karna was chariotless."}},{"n":69,"text":"रक्षन्प्रतिज्ञां च पुनर्भीमसेनकृतां पुरा ।\nविरथान्विह्वलांश्चक्रे न तु प्राणैर्व्ययोजयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Keeping again the vow once made by Bhimasena, he left them chariotless and bewildered but did not part them from their lives."}},{"n":70,"text":"भीमसेनेन तु वधः पुत्राणां ते प्रतिश्रुतः ।\nपुनर्द्यूते च पार्थेन वधः कर्णस्य संश्रुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For Bhimasena had vowed the killing of your sons, and at the second dice game Partha had vowed Karna's killing."}},{"n":71,"text":"वधे त्वकुर्वन्यत्नं ते तस्य कर्णमुखास्तदा ।\nनाशक्नुवंश्च तं हन्तुं सात्यकिं प्रवरा रथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They, led by Karna, tried to kill him then, but those best chariot-fighters could not kill Satyaki."}},{"n":72,"text":"द्रौणिश्च कृतवर्मा च तथैवान्ये महारथाः ।\nनिर्जिता धनुषैकेन शतशः क्षत्रियर्षभाः ।\nकाङ्क्षता परलोकं च धर्मराजस्य च प्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona's son, Kritavarman and other great chariot-fighters, hundreds of bull-like warriors, were beaten by that one bow, as he wished for the other world and what was dear to the king of dharma."}},{"n":73,"text":"कृष्णयोः सदृशो वीर्ये सात्यकिः शत्रुकर्शनः ।\nकृष्णो वापि भवेल्लोके पार्थो वापि धनुर्धरः ।\nशैनेयो वा नरव्याघ्रश्चतुर्थो नोपलभ्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki, tormentor of foes, equals the two Krishnas in valor; in the world there might be Krishna, or Partha the bowman, or Shaineya, bull among men, but a fourth is not found."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":74,"text":"अजय्यं रथमास्थाय वासुदेवस्य सात्यकिः ।\nविरथं कृतवान्कर्णं वासुदेवसमो युवा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mounting Vasudeva's unconquerable chariot, Satyaki, young and equal to Vasudeva, made Karna chariotless."}},{"n":75,"text":"दारुकेण समायुक्तं स्वबाहुबलदर्पितः ।\nकच्चिदन्यं समारूढः स रथं सात्यकिः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Proud of the strength of his own arms, with Daruka as his driver, did Satyaki again mount another chariot?"}},{"n":76,"text":"एतदिच्छाम्यहं श्रोतुं कुशलो ह्यसि भाषितुम् ।\nअसह्यं तमहं मन्ये तन्ममाचक्ष्व संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wish to hear this; you are skilled in speaking. I think he is irresistible; tell me, Sanjaya."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":77,"text":"शृणु राजन्यथा तस्य रथमन्यं महामतिः ।\nदारुकस्यानुजस्तूर्णं कल्पनाविधिकल्पितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear, O king, how Daruka's younger brother, of great wit, quickly brought another chariot, prepared by the proper rules for it."}},{"n":78,"text":"आयसैः काञ्चनैश्चापि पट्टैर्नद्धं सकूबरम् ।\nतारासहस्रखचितं सिंहध्वजपताकिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was bound with iron and golden plates, with a hub-covering, studded with thousands of stars, with a lion banner and flags,"}},{"n":79,"text":"अश्वैर्वातजवैर्युक्तं हेमभाण्डपरिच्छदैः ।\nपाण्डुरैरिन्दुसंकाशैः सर्वशब्दातिगैर्दृढैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"yoked with horses swift as wind, in golden trappings, white like the moon, strong and unmatched in speed,"}},{"n":80,"text":"चित्रकाञ्चनसंनाहैर्वाजिमुख्यैर्विशां पते ।\nघण्टाजालाकुलरवं शक्तितोमरविद्युतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the finest horses in colorful golden armor, lord of men, the sound of bell-nets ringing, shining with spears and lances,"}},{"n":81,"text":"वृतं सांग्रामिकैर्द्रव्यैर्बहुशस्त्रपरिच्छदम् ।\nरथं संपादयामास मेघगम्भीरनिस्वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"filled with war-equipment and many weapons, its sound deep as a cloud. He had that chariot prepared."}},{"n":82,"text":"तं समारुह्य शैनेयस्तव सैन्यमुपाद्रवत् ।\nदारुकोऽपि यथाकामं प्रययौ केशवान्तिकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mounting it, Shaineya rushed at your army, and Daruka went wherever he wished to Keshava's side."}},{"n":83,"text":"कर्णस्यापि महाराज शङ्खगोक्षीरपाण्डुरैः ।\nचित्रकाञ्चनसंनाहैः सदश्वैर्वेगवत्तरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna too, O great king, was brought a chariot with horses white as a conch or cow's milk, in colorful golden armor, excellent and very swift,"}},{"n":84,"text":"हेमकक्ष्याध्वजोपेतं कॢप्तयन्त्रपताकिनम् ।\nअग्र्यं रथं सुयन्तारं बहुशस्त्रपरिच्छदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"with golden girths and a banner, with its machines and flags set, the best of chariots with a good driver and many weapons."}},{"n":85,"text":"उपाजह्रुस्तमास्थाय कर्णोऽप्यभ्यद्रवद्रिपून् ।\nएतत्ते सर्वमाख्यातं यन्मां त्वं परिपृच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mounting it, Karna rushed at his foes. All this I have told you, as you asked me."}},{"n":86,"text":"भूयश्चापि निबोध त्वं तवापनयजं क्षयम् ।\nएकत्रिंशत्तव सुता भीमसेनेन पातिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear further about the destruction born from your own misjudgment: thirty-one of your sons were struck down by Bhimasena."}},{"n":87,"text":"दुर्मुखं प्रमुखे कृत्वा सततं चित्रयोधिनम् ।\nशतशो निहताः शूराः सात्वतेनार्जुनेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Putting Durmukha at the head, he killed hundreds of heroes, always wondrous fighters, and the Satvata and Arjuna did too."}},{"n":88,"text":"भीष्मं प्रमुखतः कृत्वा भगदत्तं च मारिष ।\nएवमेष क्षयो वृत्तो राजन्दुर्मन्त्रिते तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"With Bhishma at the front, and Bhagadatta, honorable sir, this was the destruction that came to be, O king, from your ill counsel."}}]}]}